<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97294" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρέφω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>turning round, revolving, circling</i>, of the
			constellations, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκτου στροφάδες
			κέλευθοι</span> the Bear's <i>circling</i> paths, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				131
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				594
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφάδεσσιν ἀέλλαις</span>
			<i>whirl-</i>winds, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				677
			</span></i>; of cranes <i>on their return</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				1032
			</span></i>; of fish, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφάδες παρὰ πέτρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Numen.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.319b
			</span></i>; of worms, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στροφάδες</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσοι</span>), αἱ,
				<i>the Drifting Isles</i>, a group not far from Zacynthus,
			supposed to have been once floating, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				1.9.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.4.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
